infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title What QUIC buys, and what it costs
  desc One protocol-wide trade: spend CPU per byte to win latency, evolution, and stream independence
  compares
    - label What you win
      children
        - label 1-RTT handshake
          desc Merged transport + TLS 1.3, down from TCP+TLS's 2 RTT
        - label 0-RTT resumption
          desc Reconnect on a cached session ticket with no round trip
        - label 30–55% faster on lossy mobile
          desc Page load versus HTTP/2 on a lossy cellular link
        - label Evolves in user space
          desc Ship new congestion control weekly, no OS kernel patch
        - label Independent streams
          desc A dropped packet blocks only its own stream, not all of them
    - label What it costs
      children
        - label 15–30% more CPU per byte
          desc User-space processing plus per-packet AES-GCM, versus kernel TCP
        - label No kernel offload
          desc Transport logic runs in the application, not the OS fast path
        - label Per-packet encryption
          desc Almost the entire packet is encrypted so middleboxes stay blind
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
